==Trivia==
*CTO stands for Chief Technology Officer or Chief Technical Officer.
*His Japanese name, Pawaharakko Buchō (パワハラッコ部長, "Department Chief Pawaharakko"), combines パワハラ ''pawahara'' (short for "[[wikipedia:Power harassment|power harassment]]", meaning abuse of power by a higher-up at a workplace) with 海獺 ''rakko'' (sea otter); 部長 ''buchō'' means "department chief", the equivalent of an American vice president  (of a company).
*He's actually an otter, not a seal.
**The "Seal" in his name is likely just a pun on the stamp he holds.

